.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_DATA_CREATE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_data_create_ex ,
.Nm CMS_data_create
.Nd Create CMS Data object
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo CMS_data_create_ex
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft CMS_ContentInfo *
.Fo CMS_data_create
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fa "unsigned int flags"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_data_create_ex
creates a
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure with a type
.Sy NID_pkcs7_data .
The data is supplied via the
.Fa in
BIO. The library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq
are used when retrieving algorithms from providers.
The
.Fa flags
field supports the
.Sy CMS_STREAM
flag.
Internally
.Xr CMS_final 3
is called unless
.Sy CMS_STREAM
is specified.
.Pp
The
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure can be freed using
.Xr CMS_ContentInfo_free 3 .
.Pp
.Fn CMS_data_create
is similar to
.Fn CMS_data_create_ex
but uses default values of NULL for the library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query
.Fa propq .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If the allocation fails,
.Fn CMS_data_create_ex
and
.Fn CMS_data_create
return NULL and set an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
Otherwise they return a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr CMS_final 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn CMS_data_create_ex
method was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
